    {
      "id": "product.chatgpt",
      "slug": "chatgpt",
      "name": "ChatGPT",
      "title": "ChatGPT (OpenAI)",
      "vendor": "OpenAI",
      "status": "proposal",
      "reviewed": "2026-11-22",
      "url": "https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/products/product.chatgpt.md",
      "summaryHtml": "ChatGPT lets anyone ask, talk through or hand off work in plain language, from a quick answer in Chat to a finished deliverable in Work: &quot;ChatGPT is an AI agent that you communicate with in natural language&quot;, and &quot;ChatGPT Work can plan a task, gather context, use tools, and carry the work through to a result you can review&quot; (<a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/use-chatgpt\">S1</a>). OpenAI makes it. It runs on the web, in a desktop app for macOS and Windows, with Linux &quot;in public preview&quot; since 14 August 2026, in iOS and Android apps, through a Chrome extension, in voice, and as @ChatGPT in Slack (<a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/app\">S2</a>, <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/download\">S3</a>, <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6825453-chatgpt-release-notes\">S4</a>, <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/features/voice\">S20</a>, <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/third-party/slack\">S23</a>). The desktop app also holds Codex, &quot;Choose ChatGPT or Codex&quot; (<a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/app\">S2</a>), and dots, always-on agents &quot;in the cloud&quot; with &quot;its own computer and browser&quot; (<a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots\">S7</a>). It is a hosted service sold on plans, from Free at $0 through Go, Plus and Pro, up to $500 a month, to Business and Enterprise, with Work and Codex sharing &quot;pricing, credits, and usage limits&quot;; the pages read state no licence (<a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/pricing\">S21</a>). The latest app release seen is ChatGPT for iOS 1.2026.314, of 18 November 2026 (<a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\">S5</a>), and the latest release note 20 November 2026 (<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6825453-chatgpt-release-notes\">S4</a>). Its cloud work &quot;uses the Codex task-execution harness&quot; (<a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/chatgpt-work-cloud-security\">S15</a>); it is an <a href=\"/glossary/agent-harness/\">agent harness</a> in that sense, an <a href=\"/glossary/agent-host/\">agent host</a>, since a cloud task &quot;can keep going after you close the desktop app and continue from the web or mobile app&quot; (<a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/use-chatgpt\">S1</a>), and a <a href=\"/glossary/client/\">client</a>. Its skills follow the <a href=\"/specifications/#spec-agent-skills\">Agent Skills specification</a>. Its maker's own words for it are on the vendor card <a href=\"https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/vendors/openai/openai.chatgpt.md\">ChatGPT (OpenAI)</a>.",
