      "name": "Cursor",
      "title": "Cursor (Anysphere)",
      "vendor": "Anysphere",
      "status": "proposal",
      "reviewed": "2026-11-22",
      "url": "https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/products/product.cursor.md",
      "summaryHtml": "Cursor lets developers build software with agents: &quot;Cursor is a coding agent for building ambitious software&quot;, &quot;the AI editor and coding agent&quot; (<a href=\"https://cursor.com/docs\">S1</a>). Anysphere, Inc. makes it, and on 14 August 2026 &quot;Cursor has officially been acquired by SpaceX&quot; (<a href=\"https://cursor.com/downloads\">S15</a>, <a href=\"https://cursor.com/blog/joining-spacex\">S17</a>). It runs as a desktop editor with an Agents Window, a terminal CLI, on the web, on iOS, in Slack, Linear and GitHub, and through an API (<a href=\"https://cursor.com/docs/cloud-agent\">S7</a>, <a href=\"https://cursor.com/docs/agent/agents-window\">S9</a>, <a href=\"https://cursor.com/downloads\">S15</a>). It is sold by subscription, from a free tier to Enterprise; no open-source licence was seen (<a href=\"https://cursor.com/pricing\">S16</a>). The latest desktop release seen is 3.31, undated (<a href=\"https://cursor.com/downloads\">S15</a>), and the latest CLI v2026.11.17 (<a href=\"https://cursor.com/docs/cli/changelog\">S14</a>). It is an <a href=\"/glossary/agent-harness/\">agent harness</a> and a <a href=\"/glossary/client/\">client</a>. Its skills follow the <a href=\"/specifications/#spec-agent-skills\">Agent Skills specification</a>.",
      "instanceOf": [
        {
          "id": "industry.agent-harness",
          "label": "Agent harness",
          "url": "/glossary/agent-harness/"
        },
        {
          "id": "industry.client",
