      "status": "proposal",
      "reviewed": "2026-11-22",
      "url": "https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/products/product.github-copilot-cloud-agent.md",
      "summaryHtml": "Copilot's cloud agent lets Copilot &quot;answer questions about your repositories, plan and make changes, review pull requests, and automate repository tasks&quot; without the developer's machine, an <a href=\"/glossary/agent/\">agent</a> in GitHub's cloud (<a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/concepts/agents/cloud-agent/about-cloud-agent\">S1</a>). GitHub makes it; once called Copilot coding agent, it is now part of &quot;Copilot in the cloud&quot;, whose sessions run by default in a &quot;secure cloud sandbox&quot;, &quot;one session, every surface&quot; (<a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/concepts/agents/cloud-agent/about-cloud-agent\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-work-from-anywhere-with-a-new-connected-copilot-cloud-experience/\">S2</a>). It runs in GitHub's sandbox, on GitHub Actions or on a custom environment, and tasks start from github.com, GitHub Mobile, Copilot CLI, the Copilot app, VS Code, Slack or Microsoft Teams (<a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/concepts/agents/cloud-agent/about-cloud-agent\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-work-from-anywhere-with-a-new-connected-copilot-cloud-experience/\">S2</a>). It is proprietary, on paid Copilot plans (<a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-work-from-anywhere-with-a-new-connected-copilot-cloud-experience/\">S2</a>). GitHub publishes no version numbers; the new experience became generally available from 28 October 2026 (<a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-work-from-anywhere-with-a-new-connected-copilot-cloud-experience/\">S2</a>). Its skills follow the <a href=\"/specifications/#spec-agent-skills\">Agent Skills specification</a>. Its maker's own words for it are on the vendor card <a href=\"https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/vendors/microsoft/microsoft.copilot.md\">Copilot (Microsoft)</a>.",
