    {
      "id": "product.lm-studio",
      "slug": "lm-studio",
      "name": "LM Studio",
      "title": "LM Studio (Element Labs)",
      "vendor": "Element Labs",
      "status": "proposal",
      "reviewed": "2026-11-22",
      "url": "https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/products/product.lm-studio.md",
      "summaryHtml": "LM Studio lets people download and run open models on their own computer, chat with them, and serve them to other tools: &quot;Download and run local LLMs like gpt-oss or Llama, Qwen&quot;, with a &quot;simple and flexible chat interface&quot;, MCP servers, and use as &quot;a seamless, drop-in local backend for your favorite tools&quot; (<a href=\"https://lmstudio.ai/docs/app\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://lmstudio.ai/docs/integrations\">S11</a>). Element Labs, Inc. makes it (<a href=\"https://lmstudio.ai/app-terms\">S5</a>). It runs as a desktop app on macOS, Windows and Linux, as <code>llmster</code>, a headless daemon for servers, and through the <code>lms</code> CLI (<a href=\"https://lmstudio.ai/docs/app\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://lmstudio.ai/docs/app/basics/lmstudio-vs-llmster-vs-lms\">S2</a>, <a href=\"https://lmstudio.ai/download\">S3</a>). The app is proprietary: Element Labs grants a licence &quot;solely for personal and / or internal business purposes&quot; (<a href=\"https://lmstudio.ai/app-terms\">S5</a>); the <code>lms</code> CLI is &quot;MIT Licensed&quot; (<a href=\"https://github.com/lmstudio-ai/lms\">S6</a>). The latest release seen is 0.4.28, Build 2, of 31 October 2026 (<a href=\"https://lmstudio.ai/changelog/lmstudio-v0.4.28\">S4</a>). It is a model runtime, the neighbour of <a href=\"/glossary/model/\">model</a>, with a chat <a href=\"/glossary/client/\">client</a> of its own that uses MCP tools. LM Studio Bionic, its maker's agent app, is &quot;a new, separate app from LM Studio&quot; and is not rated here (<a href=\"https://lmstudio.ai/docs/bionic\">S16</a>, <a href=\"https://lmstudio.ai/blog/introducing-lm-studio-bionic\">S17</a>).",
      "instanceOf": [
