    {
      "id": "product.minimax-code",
      "slug": "minimax-code",
      "name": "MiniMax Code",
      "title": "MiniMax Code (MiniMax)",
      "vendor": "MiniMax",
      "status": "proposal",
      "reviewed": "2026-11-22",
      "url": "https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/products/product.minimax-code.md",
      "summaryHtml": "MiniMax Code lets its users hand coding and everyday office work to an agent: &quot;From coding to office work, MiniMax Code connects to your local files, tools, and browser&quot;, in a Coding mode and a Work mode (<a href=\"https://code.minimax.io/about\">S2</a>). MiniMax presents it as &quot;The all-in-one general agent built for MiniMax models&quot; (<a href=\"https://www.minimax.io\">S1</a>), and its documentation as &quot;a desktop AI Agent app for software development, everyday workflows, automation, and remote collaboration&quot; (<a href=\"https://code.minimax.io/docs/code/welcome\">S3</a>). MiniMax makes it; it is the former MiniMax Agent desktop app, &quot;officially renamed to MiniMax Code&quot; on 29 May 2026, and its web app still lives at agent.minimax.io (<a href=\"https://code.minimax.io/docs/changelog\">S4</a>, <a href=\"https://code.minimax.io/about\">S2</a>). It runs as a desktop app for macOS and Windows, a web app, a phone companion for iOS and Android, and a terminal CLI, <code>mcode</code>, with editors reaching it over ACP (<a href=\"https://code.minimax.io/about\">S2</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/minimax-code\">S5</a>, <a href=\"https://code.minimax.io/docs/cli/integrations\">S9</a>). The CLI is open source, &quot;An open-source coding agent for your terminal, powered by MiniMax&quot;, whose &quot;First-party code defaults to MIT&quot;; the repository &quot;does not include the desktop application's source&quot; (<a href=\"https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/minimax-code\">S5</a>). It is paid through MiniMax's M Plan, shown as Go $22, Explore $55 and Build $132, with daily free credits (<a href=\"https://code.minimax.io/about\">S2</a>, <a href=\"https://code.minimax.io/docs/changelog\">S4</a>). The latest releases seen are desktop v3.1.16, of 16 November 2026, and CLI 0.7.8, of 19 November 2026, by the changelog; the CLI repository's latest GitHub release is v0.7.2, of 31 October 2026 (observed) (<a href=\"https://code.minimax.io/docs/changelog\">S4</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/minimax-code\">S5</a>). MiniMax's home page also presents MiniMax Design, and its web changelog presents MaxClaw and MaxHermes, &quot;A cloud-based AI assistant built on Hermes Agent&quot; (<a href=\"https://www.minimax.io\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://code.minimax.io/docs/changelog\">S4</a>). It is an <a href=\"/glossary/agent-harness/\">agent harness</a> and a <a href=\"/glossary/client/\">client</a>.",
      "instanceOf": [
        {
          "id": "industry.agent-harness",
          "label": "Agent harness",
          "url": "/glossary/agent-harness/"
        },
