      "reviewed": "2026-11-22",
      "url": "https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/products/product.orca.md",
      "summaryHtml": "Orca lets one person run many coding agents side by side, each in its own git worktree: &quot;the agent development environment&quot;, &quot;a desktop IDE for running multiple AI coding agents side by side&quot; (<a href=\"https://github.com/stablyai/orca\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://orca.dev/\">S2</a>). Stably AI makes it, backed by Y Combinator, in the <code>stablyai</code> GitHub organisation (<a href=\"https://github.com/stablyai/orca\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://orca.dev/\">S2</a>). It is an <a href=\"/glossary/agent-host/\">agent host</a> for other makers' agent CLIs and a <a href=\"/glossary/client/\">client</a> onto their sessions: an Electron desktop app for macOS, Windows and Linux, a phone companion, remote Orca servers, SSH machines and cloud VMs, and the <code>orca</code> CLI (<a href=\"https://github.com/stablyai/orca\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://orca.dev/\">S2</a>, S10). It is MIT open source and free; its agents run on &quot;the Claude Code or Codex you already pay for&quot; (<a href=\"https://github.com/stablyai/orca\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://orca.dev/\">S2</a>). The latest release seen is v1.4.269, of 21 November 2026, the version installed on sol (<a href=\"https://github.com/stablyai/orca/releases/tag/v1.4.269\">S7</a>, S10). Its maker's own words for it are on the vendor cards <a href=\"https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/vendors/orca/orca.app.md\">Orca app (Orca)</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/vendors/orca/orca.runtime.md\">Orca runtime (Orca)</a>.",
