    {
      "id": "product.paperclip",
      "slug": "paperclip",
      "name": "Paperclip",
      "title": "Paperclip (Paperclip Labs)",
      "vendor": "Paperclip Labs",
      "status": "proposal",
      "reviewed": "2026-11-22",
      "url": "https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/products/product.paperclip.md",
      "summaryHtml": "Paperclip lets one person run a company of AI agents, with &quot;org charts, budgets, goals, governance, and accountability&quot;: &quot;the app people use to manage AI agents for work&quot; (<a href=\"https://paperclip.ing\">S1</a>). Paperclip Labs, Inc. makes it, in the <code>paperclipai</code> GitHub organisation; it is &quot;a Node.js server and React UI that orchestrates a team of AI agents to run a business&quot;, whose agents are other makers' harnesses such as Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Cursor, OpenCode, Pi and Hermes (<a href=\"https://paperclip.ing\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip\">S2</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.paperclip.ing/reference/adapters/overview/\">S5</a>). It runs self-hosted &quot;as a local instance or a remote deploy&quot;, started from the <code>paperclipai</code> CLI, with a web board that phones can install as a standalone app, and a waitlist for a hosted app (<a href=\"https://paperclip.ing\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip\">S2</a>, <a href=\"https://paperclip.ing/changelog/v2026.1117.0/\">S4</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.paperclip.ing/reference/deploy/deployment-modes/\">S19</a>). It is MIT open source, &quot;self-hosted, no Paperclip account required&quot; (<a href=\"https://paperclip.ing\">S1</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip\">S2</a>). The latest release seen is v2026.1117.0, of 17 November 2026; the repository's Releases section is empty (<a href=\"https://paperclip.ing/changelog/\">S3</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip\">S2</a>). It is an <a href=\"/glossary/agent-host/\">agent host</a> and a <a href=\"/glossary/client/\">client</a>.",
      "instanceOf": [
        {
          "id": "industry.agent-host",
          "label": "Agent host",
          "url": "/glossary/agent-host/"
        },
        {
          "id": "industry.client",
          "label": "Client",
          "url": "/glossary/client/"
        }
