  "glossary": [
    {
      "id": "industry.model",
      "slug": "model",
      "kind": "industry",
      "label": "Model",
      "status": "agreed",
      "url": "/glossary/model/",
      "cardUrl": "https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/industry/industry.model.md",
      "summaryHtml": "A model is what decides: the one thing every other layer of an agentic system is built from.",
      "bodyHtml": "<p>A model is what decides: the one thing every other layer of an agentic system is built from.</p>\n<p>A model, in agentic systems a large language model (LLM), takes text and images in and gives text out. It acts on nothing by itself: it reads no file, runs no command and keeps nothing from one call to the next.</p>\n<h3>Our conventions</h3>\n<p>The Knowledge Islands system uses &quot;model&quot; in this sense and has no convention of its own to map onto it.</p>\n<h3>Next</h3>\n<p>The <a href=\"/glossary/agent-harness/\">agent harness</a> turns a model into an agent.</p>",
      "instances": []
    },
    {
      "id": "industry.agent-harness",
      "slug": "agent-harness",
      "kind": "industry",
      "label": "Agent harness",
      "status": "agreed",
      "url": "/glossary/agent-harness/",
      "cardUrl": "https://github.com/knowledgeislands/ki-agent-backpack/blob/75dd86fbff11a33b551fbd9d37b9d0576b1f9598/skills/keystone/ki-agentic-ecosystems/knowledge/industry/industry.agent-harness.md",
      "summaryHtml": "An agent harness turns a <a href=\"/glossary/model/\">model</a> into an agent, so that what the model decides is carried out in the world.",
      "bodyHtml": "<p>An agent harness turns a <a href=\"/glossary/model/\">model</a> into an agent, so that what the model decides is carried out in the world.</p>\n<p>It is software that runs the loop: it gives the model its context, carries out the tool calls the model asks for, and feeds the results back until the work is done. It holds the tools, handles the context as it grows, and keeps each run it carries out. The model decides; the harness acts.</p>\n<p>Vendor text often writes &quot;harness&quot; for the harness and the agent together; read it as covering both layers unless the text separates them.</p>\n<h3>Our conventions</h3>\n<p>A territory's bundle of skills, subagents, evals and hooks, such as the <code>ki-agent-backpack</code> repository, is not an agent harness: it runs no loop and calls no model. Under INDUSTRY-FIRST it has its own name, a <a href=\"/glossary/backpack/\">backpack</a> (HARNESS-NAME); never call it a harness.</p>\n<p>Knowledge Islands names an agent harness by one of six values: <code>claude-code</code>; <code>codex</code>; <code>gemini</code>; <code>claude-chat</code>, Claude's own chat loop in Claude Desktop or claude.ai, Cowork included; <code>claude-design</code>; and <code>chatgpt</code>, ChatGPT's own loop, voice included. The Cairn store's roster records each agent <a href=\"/glossary/actor/\">actor</a>'s agent harness as <code>ki-harness</code>, beside the application it runs in as <code>ki-host</code> (PRESENCE-FIELDS a), so one harness keeps one value wherever it runs.</p>\n<h3>Next</h3>\n<p>The <a href=\"/glossary/agent/\">agent</a> is a model working through an agent harness.</p>",
      "instances": [
        {
          "slug": "antigravity",
          "name": "Antigravity",
          "vendor": "Google"
        },
